  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-BRA101</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved employment policies and business models to facilitate the adoption of measures towards decent work in selected supply chains and states, targeting vulnerable workers and youth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2023, external pressures intensified, marked by persistent conflicts in Eastern Europe and emerging conflicts in the Gaza Strip. These geopolitical tensions compounded inflationary shocks stemming from COVID-19 imbalances and internal crises within retail companies. In Brazil, the new government faced hurdles in advancing its agenda due to opposition parties holding a legislative majority, hindering the promotion of public policies aimed at economic growth and poverty reduction.

Brazil&apos;s economic recovery, evident after the peak of the COVID-19 pandemic, saw growth in GDP and employment. In 2023, GDP increased by 2.9%, with the employed population reaching 101 million, the highest since 2012. However, informality and low wages persist, with 39.5 million workers in informal employment and an average real remuneration of R$3,134. Addressing informality and improving labor conditions, including combating child and forced labor, remains crucial for social justice and a fairer future.

The ILO Office for Brazil plans strategic collaboration with Brazilian constituents over the next two years to promote labor rights. Initiatives include relaunching the Sustainable Work Program, developing a national employment strategy, and promoting responsible business practices. Additionally, efforts focus on green job knowledge, ecological transformation, national REDD+ strategy, and dialogue spaces involving indigenous peoples, aiming for a just transition with a gender perspective and adherence to Convention 169.</narrative>
  </description>
